1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Large VLAs think in chunks. Inference delay stalls the robot.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:26,000
If the robot waits, motion stalls. We measure that on AMD ROCm.

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:40,000
We fine-tune on AMD and execute with latency-aware chunking.

4
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,333
Task: pick the fruit and place it in the basket.

5
00:00:48,333 --> 00:01:01,667
SmolVLA Sync places successfully at native AMD latency.

6
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:15,000
Formal Sync-full result: two place successes out of twenty.

7
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:28,333
Same protocol at +200 ms: Sync freezes on every replan.

8
00:01:28,333 --> 00:01:41,667
Under delay, Sync place success collapses to zero.

9
00:01:41,667 --> 00:01:55,000
Async keeps acting while the next chunk is computed.

10
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:09,000
On this static task, Async beats RTC on place. We report that honestly.

11
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:22,333
RTC removes freezes, but guidance did not raise place success.

12
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:34,333
Expert-only π0.5 failed; unfreezing vision unlocked a place.

13
00:02:34,333 --> 00:02:47,667
Here is the π0.5 B1d place success under Sync-full.

14
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:58,667
Env-B shifts the fruit 3 to 5 centimeters at eval time only.

15
00:02:58,667 --> 00:03:12,000
The Env-A place winner fails under its paired Env-B shift.

16
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Under +200 ms, Async recovers place and lift versus Sync freeze.

17
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:30,000
RTC continuity helps; place success stays below Async here.

18
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Vision unfreeze is what unlocked π0.5 closed-loop grasp.

19
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Held-out 3–5 cm shift zeros place for both policies.

20
00:03:47,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Numbers from frozen formal eval — no invented gains.

21
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Code, technical report, and demo video are in the submission.
